Pure lifecycle interface regression, 2026-09-16.
Authority: EvoIR module registrations and shared program state; no new rule.
RED: an empty registered constructor or destructor lowered with no mem/world
interface and failed existing validation: E3101 invalid lifecycle registration.
Repair: resolved registrations join the existing function participant set;
the same registrations then construct the module table. Validator unchanged.

Focused test: pure_lifecycle_handlers_still_participate_in_program_effect_threading.
Constructor/destructor, before/after/on-definition attributes, C-HIR/EvoIR/asm.
All 18 checks pass; the two complete lifecycle/inline test groups pass 26/26.

Native fixture: elf-pure-lifecycle.c.
The subject assembly contains before in .init_array.00201,
on_definition in .init_array.00202 and after in .fini_array.00201.
GCC-14 and Clang-19 each assemble/link it with -Wl,--gc-sections; both exit 0.
Both fixed compilers also compile/run the source at -std=gnu11 -O0/-O2: exit 0.
Clang reports -Wignored-attributes for the late destructor declaration.
That source control does not prove registration equivalence; the project's
existing declaration-chain rule governs the subject's retained registration.
Empty bodies make native exit alone insufficient; emitted registrations and
EvoIR validation explicitly check the missing interface which caused the RED.

Environment: evo-flight-lab:sealed, ARM64, network none;
image 2c23684c9cc5ef5899073b59844fa47cc3c1d894f2316e21f25d5d85be5a10e2.
GCC 14.2.0-19, Clang 19.1.7.
Reproduce:
  CARGO_TARGET_DIR=target/frontend cargo test -p evocc --offline -j1 \
    --test elf_lifecycles --test inline_definition_roles
  target/frontend/debug/evocc --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu --emit=asm \
    tests/fixtures/elf-pure-lifecycle.c > /tmp/elf-pure-lifecycle.s
  # In the fixed ARM64 image, for gcc-14 and clang-19:
  gcc-14 -Wl,--gc-sections elf-pure-lifecycle.s -o pure && ./pure

Separate exploratory boundary, not a compiler fix: an initial test assumed
used/retain on any redeclaration forced emission. It was withdrawn after 48
fixed-oracle object probes and the spec audit: retain is not blanket emission,
and late attributes differ between compilers. No production retention change
or gate-PASS claim is based on that withdrawn expectation.

